// functional form of 1D convolution for classical convoutional networks, not to be confused with the nn::Conv1d module which is for use in neural network architectures. The functional form is for users who want to apply a convolution operation without having to define a full module, and is intended for use in more flexible or dynamic contexts where defining a module might be too rigid. The functional form will be pluss::conv1d(...) and will take the input tensor, weight tensor, bias tensor (optional), stride, padding, dilation, and groups as arguments. It will perform the convolution operation using the specified parameters and return the output tensor. The implementation will be optimized for performance and will support various data types and devices as supported by the underlying tensor library.
// Example usage: Series output = pluss::conv1d(input, weight, bias, stride, padding, dilation, groups);
